# PRD-005a: `cp .env.example .env` holds AGENTCAD_SECRET_KEY. It is in
# .dockerignore so it never lands in an image layer; this keeps it out of the
# repository for the same reason. `.env.*` too — `.env.prod`, `.env.staging`
# and `.env.local` are the ordinary way to keep two deployments apart, and the
# one carrying the production secret is exactly the one that must not be
# committed. `!.env.example` keeps the checked-in template visible.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
